INSERT INTO characters (slug,name,team,creator,owner_id,tags,appears_in,data,url_slug,status,updated_at,created_at) VALUES
('o-horseman','O. Horseman','demon','legitch',NULL,'','SCP Fragmented Veil','{"slug":"o-horseman","name":"O. Horseman","team":"demon","ability":"You & all Minions have a quest. On completion, that player evolves into their Demon marked on script (you keep your ability) & all players learn which.","creator":"legitch","appearsIn":"SCP Fragmented Veil","lede":"SCP-3456 are the the horsemen of the apocalypse, arriving during moments of cataclysm, disasters, and misfortune among-st humans. They are soulless, cunning, merciless, and masochistic, with the caveat that they require a ritual to complete in order to draw out their powers.","summaryBullets":["The O. Horseman imposes quests onto their entire team, and upon completion, the reward is transforming into a specific Demon.","Players with a quest know what it is, but they might also learn additional information for the quest''s benefit.","Each Minion and the O. Horseman is marked on the script with a Demon that they always transform into.","Players with a quest don''t know how much progress they''ve made.","When the quest is completed, the victor becomes their Demon immediately, but the presence of this exact Demon will not be announced until dawn.","If the O. Horseman transforms, they still keep their ability and thus the quests alongside it.","Minions that transform into Demons now register as a Demon, and thus must be killed alongside the O. Horseman for good to win.","If the O. Horseman is drunk or poisoned when a quest is complete, the victor does not transform into the Demon, and it''s presence will not be announced.","If a Minion becomes another character type, they lose their quest, and if the reverse occurs, they gain a new quest when they wake."],"howToRun":["On the script, place a mark on each Minion and the O. Horseman that corresponds to a Demon they''ll transform into once their quest is complete.","While setting up the game, decide what quest the O. Horseman and each Minion has, and write them on a piece of paper, or on a phone.","During the first night, wake the Demon. Show their quest, then put them to sleep. Repeat this for each Minion as-well. Mark the evil team with the O. Horseman''s **PROGRESS CLOCK** reminder token.","Note that quests in it of themselves can provide additional information, such as which player has which character, or which character is in-play, if it pertains to the quest.","Each time a player with a quest advances in it, rotate the **PROGRESS CLOCK** reminder near their character token by a certain amount of degrees so that once the quest is fully complete, it completes a full rotation {{i|(Ex. If a quest requires 2 certain players be executed, the reminder token will be rotated 180° degrees with each advancement. If a quest requires 3 phrases be said by the player during the day, the reminder token will be rotated 120° degrees with each advancement)}}. Additionally, use the O. Horseman’s **?** reminders if you need to.","Upon a complete rotation of a **PROGRESS CLOCK** reminder, replace that token with the **TRANSFORMED** reminder token, if it''s the O. Horseman, also mark them with the **KEEPS ABILITY**. Wake that player, show them the **YOU ARE** info token, then their new Demon character token, then put them to sleep. Replace their old character token with the new Demon character token indicate as a mark on the script.","Each dawn, if a Demon player is marked with the O. Horseman''s **TRANSFORMED** reminder, declare that this Demon is in-play, then remove that reminder {{i|(if needed, also detail what their ability)}}."],"tips":["**Optional rule:** only living Minions pertain their quest and can evolve into Demons. {{i|(This is the original intent of the O. Horseman.)}}"],"quote":"It stopped soon as my flare reached its highest point, and turned. It looked straight down at me, both the horse and the... thing, on its back. It smiled, and for the first time in my life, I felt utter despair and ruin. Calamity stepped foot through the gates of heaven, ready for another world to destroy.","iconBy":"le_nuberto","jinxes":[{"name":"Engineer","align":"good","text":"Minions-turned-Demons cannot be affected by the Engineer.","id":"engineer"},{"name":"Fang Gu","align":"evil","text":"When a Minion becomes the Fang Gu after completing their quest, one Townsfolk might become an Outsider.","id":"fanggu"},{"name":"Kazali","align":"evil","text":"When a Minion becomes the Kazali after completing their quest, Minions & other Demons wake the same night to choose which Minion & Demon characters they''d like to be.","id":"kazali"},{"name":"Legion","align":"evil","text":"When a Minion becomes the Legion after completing their quest, one player becomes an evil Legion.","id":"legion"},{"name":"Leviathan","align":"evil","text":"When a Minion becomes the Leviathan after completing their quest, if its after Day 5, there is 1 more day before evil wins.","id":"leviathan"},{"name":"Lil'' Monsta","align":"evil","text":"When a Minion becomes the Lil'' Monsta after completing their quest, they keep their original Minion character.","id":"lilmonsta"},{"name":"Minstrel","align":"good","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Minstrel.","id":"minstrel"},{"name":"Riot","align":"evil","text":"The Minions-turned-Riot''s ability cannot win the game, but is still active even if they die.","id":"riot"},{"name":"Town Crier","align":"good","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Town Crier.","id":"towncrier"},{"name":"Vigormortis","align":"evil","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Vigormortis. If the Minion that could become the Vigormortis is in-play, one Outsider might be replaced with a Townsfolk.","id":"vigormortis"},{"name":"▼","align":"evil","text":"When a Minion becomes the ∇ after completing their quest, any Minions & Demons might become ones from the Trouble Brewing set.","slug":"scp-1936"},{"name":"Ball o'' Death","align":"good","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Ball o'' Death.","slug":"ball-o-death"},{"name":"Cespholopod","align":"evil","text":"If the Minion that could become the Cespholopod is in-play, Minions & the Demon do not learn each other and one extra Minion is in-play.","slug":"cespholopod"},{"name":"Eyeceue","align":"evil","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Eyeceue. When a Minion becomes the Eyeceue after completing their quest, they keep their original Minion character.","slug":"eyeceue"},{"name":"Haedlaite","align":"evil","text":"When a Minion becomes the Haedlaite after completing their quest, one Minion becomes a Haedlaite but still registers as a Minion.","slug":"haedlaite"},{"name":"Hartudeztroi","align":"good","text":"If the Minion that could become the Hartudeztroi is in-play, one Minion is replaced with an Outsider and one Townsfolk might be replaced with an Outsider. If they die before they transform from their quest, one Outsider becomes an evil Minion.","id":"hartudeztroi_scp_fragmented_veil"},{"name":"Lettucbaken","align":"evil","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Lettucbaken. Players are only told when a new Demon is made rather than what Demon it is.","slug":"lettucbaken"},{"name":"Navigator","align":"good","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Navigator.","slug":"navigator-scp-fragmented-veil"},{"name":"Pecks","align":"evil","text":"When a Minion becomes the Pecks after completing their quest, all other evil players become a Pecks, then revert back to their previous character once the original Pecks dies.","slug":"pecks"},{"name":"Prognosticator","align":"good","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Prognosticator.","slug":"prognosticator"},{"name":"Sauelsuesor","align":"good","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Sauelsuesor.","slug":"sauelsuesor"},{"name":"Watislujv","align":"evil","text":"A Minion-turned-Watislujv will register any Minion as a good Minion.","slug":"watislujv"},{"name":"What Knife?","align":"evil","text":"If the Minion that could become the What Knife? is in-play, Minions think they are good characters, even if they become a Demon.","slug":"what-knife"},{"name":"xX_2662_Xx","align":"evil","text":"When a Minion becomes the xX_2662_Xx after completing their quest, only the Minion is alerted to this, and not all players.","slug":"xx-2662-xx"},{"name":"Au’Wre","align":"evil","text":"If the Minion that could become the Au''wre is in-play, Minions & the Demon do not learn each other until that player dies.","id":"auwre_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Cawthane","align":"evil","text":"If the Minion that could become the Cawthane would be in-play, they are replaced with an Outsider, and the O'' Horseman gets their quest. When completed, they get to choose which player to make an evil Cawthane.","id":"cawthane_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Fencer","align":"good","text":"The Fencer learns of all the Demon choices as opposed to just the O. Horsemen''s.","id":"fencer_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Ketos","align":"evil","text":"If the Minion that could become the Ketos is in-play, one Outsider might be replaced with a Townsfolk. When they become the Ketos after completing their quest, if its after Day 5, there is 1 more day before evil wins.","id":"ketos_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Candlemaker","align":"good","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Candlemaker.","id":"candlemaker_circus_music"},{"name":"Tiresias","align":"good","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Seer. If the Minion that could become the Seer is in-play, they don''t get any Minion info.","id":"tiresias_circus_music"},{"name":"Qiong Qi","align":"evil","text":"When a Minion becomes the Qiong Qi after completing their quest, one Townsfolk might become an Outsider.","id":"qiongqi_festival_of_lanterns"},{"name":"Tao Tie","align":"evil","text":"When a Minion becomes the Taotie after completing their quest, one Townsfolk might become an Outsider.","id":"taotie"},{"name":"Tao Wu","align":"evil","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Tao Wu. If the Minion that could become the Tao Wu is in-play, the Demon goes not get the Demon info until that player dies.","id":"taowu_festival_of_lanterns"},{"name":"Cacophony","align":"evil","text":"When a Minion becomes the Cacophony after completing their quest, one Townsfolk might become an Outsider.","id":"cacophony_2tfafullcharacterlist"},{"name":"Fawn","align":"evil","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Fawn.","id":"fawn_2tfafullcharacterlist"},{"name":"Furze-Burner","align":"good","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Furze-Burner.","id":"furzeburner_2tfafullcharacterlist"},{"name":"Olalla","align":"evil","text":"When a Minion becomes the Olalla after completing their quest, one Townsfolk might become an Outsider.","id":"olalla_2tfafullcharacterlist"},{"name":"Rat-Catcher","align":"good","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Rat-Catcher.","id":"ratcatcher_2tfafullcharacterlist"},{"name":"Troll","align":"good","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Rat-Catcher.","id":"troll_2tfafullcharacterlist"},{"name":"Cataphractos","align":"evil","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Cataphractos.","id":"cataphractos_mistfitsreleased"},{"name":"Haerbrake","align":"evil","text":"If the Minion that could become the Haerbrake is in-play, one Outsider might be replaced with a Townsfolk.","id":"haerbrake_mistfitsreleased"},{"name":"Switchblame","align":"evil","text":"When a Minion becomes the Switchblame after completing their quest, if its after Day 4, there is 1 more day before evil wins.","id":"switchblame_mistfitsreleased"},{"name":"Aunemoia","align":"evil","text":"When a Minion becomes the Aunemoia after completing their quest, one Townsfolk might become an Outsider.","id":"aunemoia_darkartists_stuff"},{"name":"Badoch","align":"evil","text":"When a Minion would''ve become the Badoch after completing their quest, no player learns this.","id":"badoch_darkartists_stuff"},{"name":"Daivout","align":"good","text":"When a Minion would become the Daivout after completing their quest, instead, something very bad happens to the good team.","id":"daivout_darkartists_stuff"},{"name":"Don Juan","align":"evil","text":"When a Minion becomes the Don Juan after completing their quest, one Townsfolk might become an Outsider.","id":"donjuan_darkartists_stuff"},{"name":"Dreydra","align":"evil","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Dreydra.","id":"dreydra_darkartists_stuff"},{"name":"Faurein","align":"evil","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Faurein. If the Minion that could become the Faurein is in-play, they think they are an Outsider, and a Minion controls their ability actions.","id":"faurein_darkartists_stuff"},{"name":"Fencer","align":"good","text":"Minions-turned-Demons still register as Minions to the Fencer.","id":"fencer_darkartists_stuff"},{"name":"Oivasyr","align":"evil","text":"If the Minion that could become the Oivasyr is in-play, one Outsider might be replaced with a Townsfolk.","id":"oivasyr_darkartists_stuff"},{"name":"Plea","align":"evil","text":"When a Minion becomes the Plea after completing their quest, one Townsfolk might become an Outsider.","id":"plea_darkartists_stuff"}],"firstNight":12.3456,"otherNight":92.3456,"reminders":["Progress clock","Transformed"],"remindersGlobal":["Progress clock","Progress clock","Progress clock","Transformed","Transformed","Transformed","Keeps ability","?","?","?"],"setup":true,"firstNightReminder":"For you and each Minion player, wake them, show them their quest.","otherNightReminder":"If the O. Horseman or a Minion completed their quest and transformed into their Demon: Announce which Demon is now in-play.","art":"art/o-horseman.png","jsonId":"ohorseman_scp_fragmented_veil","curata":false}','scp-fragmented-veil/o-horseman','published',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('what-knife','What Knife?','demon','legitch',NULL,'','SCP Fragmented Veil','{"slug":"what-knife","name":"What Knife?","team":"demon","ability":"Each night*, choose a player: they die. After day 3, you may publicly choose a living player: all other players choose if their team wins or loses.","creator":"legitch","appearsIn":"SCP Fragmented Veil","lede":"SCP-4955 makes an accusation that their wielder is someone else.","summaryBullets":["Once Day 3 has come to dusk, the Demon may choose to publicly choose a living player at any time to accuse as their true master.","This public accusation can occur at any time, including the day, night, and even when the Demon is about to be executed.","When this occurs, everything else in the game stops, and all players then congregate on choosing if the accused will win or lose.","This choice is similar to the Fiddler, in that this disregards any vote modification, restrictions, or disruption, no one can use their abilities henceforth, and also that in a tie, the evil team wins.","The Demon is also free to never make this public accusation for whatever reason."],"howToRun":["Each dusk, update the **PAST DAY** reminder for the What Knife?. If they''re marked with the **PAST DAY 2** reminder, replace it with the **PAST DAY 3** reminder. If they''re marked with the **PAST DAY 1** reminder, replace it with the **PAST DAY 2** reminder. If not marked at all with either, mark them with the **PAST DAY 1** reminder.","Each night except the first, wake the What Knife?. They point at any player. That player {{i|dies}} - mark them with the **DEAD** reminder. Put the What Knife? to sleep.","At any time past Day 3, the What Knife? may publicly choose a player. Declare that they are accused of being the true evil-doer. After a minute or two, run a “vote” for that player to win the game {{i|(this is not an execution vote.)}} All players may vote, no matter what. If the majority of players vote in favour, their team wins, if not, their team loses, either way, the game ends. On a tie, the evil team wins, regardless of the player chosen."],"iconBy":"le_nuberto","firstNight":0,"otherNight":49.4955,"reminders":["Dead","Past day 1","Past day 2","Past day 3"],"setup":false,"otherNightReminder":"This Demon points to a player. That player dies.","art":"art/what-knife.png","jsonId":"whatknife_scp_fragmented_veil","curata":false}','scp-fragmented-veil/what-knife','published',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('salvation','Salvation','demon','katsitsanoron',NULL,'','SCP Fragmented Veil','{"slug":"salvation","name":"Salvation","team":"demon","ability":"If you are executed, your team wins. The Storyteller can break the game rules, and if executed, good wins. [1 Minion is good & doesn''t get evil info]","creator":"katsitsanoron","appearsIn":"SCP Fragmented Veil","lede":"SCP-5000 must make their way to salvation as the entire world is flipped on it''s head.","summaryBullets":["With the Salvation in play, one Minion is good and doesn''t join their team.","The good Minion doesn''t know the evil team, and neither do they. However, one less starting Minion is a dead giveaway to the evil team that something isn''t right.","Good wins if the Storyteller is executed. Any living player may nominate the Storyteller, and the Storyteller is executed if 50% or more of the living players vote.","Evil wins if just two players are alive or the Salvation is executed.","If the Salvation is not in play and the Storyteller is executed, evil wins.","The Storyteller may break any of the game’s rules. They may kill a player who nominated to simulate a Witch curse, kill players at night to simulate a Demon attacking, give players false information to simulate drunkenness, change characters at night to simulate a Pit-Hag, or even have the wrong number of Outsiders in play."],"howToRun":["While setting up the game, prepare one Minion you want to be good.","During the first night, wake them. Show the **YOU ARE** info token, then give a thumbs up. Put them to sleep. During the first night''s Minion Info and Demon Info steps, the good Minion will not be included - they will not receive any information regarding who the other Minions are or who the Demon is, nor will the other Minions and Demon know who the good Minion is.","If the Salvation is executed, declare that the game ends and evil wins.","Break any game rules, as you see fit. Use evil reminder tokens if you need them."],"tips":["The Salvation is an enigmatic and complex character, and is recommended for highly experienced Storytellers. In addition to rules knowledge, it requires you to have a good sense of fun and fairness. It is your job to create a fun game for all players, so only break the game rules to give false information (as much or as little as you want) or simulate the actions of evil characters that could be in play, but aren’t. If you can convince the players that there is no the Salvation in play, or at least get them discussing the possibility, you’ve done well.","Avoid creating arbitrary rules or changing the win conditions. In order to have a good time, the players need to know how they can win the game if the Salvation is in play."],"iconBy":"le_nuberto","firstNight":1.5,"otherNight":35.5,"reminders":["Dead","Dead"],"setup":true,"firstNightReminder":"Show a Minion the ''You are'' card and a thumbs up good signal.","otherNightReminder":"More than likely, you''ll choose a player or two, those player(s) dies.","art":"art/salvation.png","jsonId":"salvation_scp_fragmented_veil","curata":false}','scp-fragmented-veil/salvation','published',datetime('now'),datetime('now'));
